# Canonical capability chains — the SINGLE source of truth for which
# upstream models the proxy walks for each tier.
#
# SP-LLM-SINGLE-SOURCE-OF-TRUTH (2026-05-05): every model-selection
# decision in the project flows from these four lines.  Both the
# local proxy and the GitHub Actions workflow (which reads this file
# via ``set -a; source chains.env; set +a``) pick up the same
# definition.  No more drift between local and CI.
#
# SP-CHAINS-SINGLE-SOURCE (2026-06-21): this file is AUTHORITATIVE — the
# proxy reads it LAST in its env_file order, so a per-machine ``.env``
# can no longer shadow these four chains (the old ``FEROVA_MODEL_*``
# alias is gone).  To change a chain, even on one machine, edit it HERE.
# An explicit ``os.environ`` value still wins (CI ``source``s this file,
# so the value matches).
#
# Format: ``provider/model[,provider/model,...]`` — comma-separated
# chain walked left-to-right on rate-limit / error / parse failure.
# The proxy's ``ModelRouter`` classifies inbound requests by substring
# (``opus`` / ``sonnet`` / ``haiku`` / ``coder``) on the alias the
# client sent and dispatches to the matching slot.
#
# Ordering rationale (2026-05-26, SP-CHAINS-THINKING-AUDIT):
#   1. **Only NO_THINKING models** — entries are restricted to models
#      empirically verified to NOT emit spontaneous ``reasoning_content``
#      / ``thinking_delta`` on a max_tokens=80 probe.  Models that
#      think spontaneously (Kimi K2.6, GLM-5.1, Qwen3.5-397B, GPT-OSS,
#      DeepSeek on direct/OpenRouter) are excluded because they consume
#      the entire output budget on internal reasoning and produce
#      whitespace-only text, triggering the peek_for_content failover
#      loop and causing 25s+ client timeouts.
#   2. NIM strips thinking for some models (DeepSeek V4 Pro, Qwen3.5,
#      Qwen3-Coder-480B) but NOT for others (Kimi K2.6, GPT-OSS-20B).
#      The same model can be NO_THINKING on NIM but THINKING on
#      OpenRouter/DeepSeek-direct.  Provider matters.
#   3. Mistral models never think on any provider — they are the only
#      family safe for cross-provider failover.
#   4. Each chain ENDS with the corresponding Anthropic model via
#      ``claude_code/<tier>`` — last-resort fallback.
#   5. **NIM-first ordering (2026-05-31)** — every chain LEADS with a
#      NIM entry; ``open_router/`` entries are retained as a demoted
#      cross-provider fallback (not removed). This restores the
#      documented per-tier intent above and avoids burning a wasted hop
#      on OpenRouter when NIM is healthy. OpenRouter credit exhaustion
#      now fails over cleanly to the next entry instead of being served
#      as content (SP-PROXY-402-FAILOVER, #286), so keeping it as a
#      fallback is safe.
#   6. **Mistral-lead override (2026-06-09, SP-CHAINS-MISTRAL-LEAD)** —
#      the SONNET/OPUS NIM heads (qwen3.5-122b, deepseek-v4-pro) began
#      LEAKING THINKING (HTTP 200 but EMPTY content — token budget burned
#      on hidden reasoning), tripping the peek_for_content failover loop
#      into 25s+ / >70s cascades, and 502s on /v1/agent (the native-tools
#      filter drops the claude_code emulation fallback). Per rule #1 (only
#      NO_THINKING) and #3 (Mistral never thinks), both tiers now LEAD with
#      a warm Mistral; the old heads stay as demoted fallbacks for when NIM
#      stabilises. Probe BOTH latency and non-empty content before
#      promoting a model back to the head.
#
# Audit data: tmp/provider_audit.py (2026-05-26 live probe, 7 providers
# × 20+ models).  Next refresh: docs/benchmarks/2026-05-26_*.json.
#
# Benchmark references:
#   - docs/benchmarks/2026-05-07_llm_chain_candidates.json (base snapshot)
#   - Artificial Analysis, Chatbot Arena, BenchLM (2026-05-26 live fetch)

# REASONER/OPUS — heavy reasoning + frontier quality.
#   1. Mistral Medium 3.5   NO_THINKING everywhere — warm-Mistral lead (see #6)
#   2. Mistral Large 3 675B NO_THINKING everywhere — opus-tier, demoted (cold 2026-06-09)
#   3. DeepSeek V4 Pro      SWE-V 80.6 — demoted: thinking-leak / timeout 2026-06-09
# Tail: claude_code/opus (claude-opus-4-7 @ SWE-V 87.6 / GPQA-D 94.2)
MODEL_OPUS=nvidia_nim/z-ai/glm-5.2,open_router/z-ai/glm-5.2,claude_code/opus

# BALANCED/SONNET — analyst / reviewer / structured-JSON default.
#   1. Mistral Medium 3.5   AA Intel 39 / 146 tps — NO_THINKING — warm lead (see #6)
#   2. Qwen3.5 122B A10B    AA Intel 42 / 145 tps — demoted: thinking-leak 2026-06-09
#   3. Mistral Small 4 119B AA Intel 28 / 169 tps — NO_THINKING everywhere (OR fallback)
# Tail: claude_code/sonnet (claude-sonnet-4-6 @ SWE-V 79.6)
MODEL_SONNET=nvidia_nim/minimaxai/minimax-m3,open_router/qwen/qwen3.7-max,open_router/minimax/minimax-m3,nvidia_nim/deepseek-ai/deepseek-v4-pro,open_router/deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro,deepseek/deepseek-v4-pro,nvidia_nim/moonshotai/kimi-k2.6,open_router/moonshotai/kimi-k2.6,kimi/kimi-k2.6,claude_code/sonnet

# CHEAP/HAIKU — short-form summaries, high-volume, low-latency.
#   1. Mistral Small 4 119B NO_THINKING everywhere — best available
#      non-thinking model for the HAIKU budget (AA Intel 28, 169 tps).
#      All former candidates (GPT-OSS-20B, Llama 4 Scout, DeepSeek V4
#      Flash) are either THINKING on NIM, removed from NIM, or not
#      loaded as providers (Groq deferred).
# Tail: claude_code/haiku (claude-haiku-4-5 @ SWE-V 73.3)
MODEL_HAIKU=nvidia_nim/z-ai/glm-5.2,open_router/qwen/qwen3.7-max,open_router/z-ai/glm-5.2,nvidia_nim/mistralai/mistral-medium-3.5-128b,open_router/mistralai/mistral-medium-3-5,claude_code/haiku
